---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { u } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  title="Financial aid"
  description="Aid year 2026-27 at the University of Mars: verification, required documents, holds, and key dates."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Student Financial Services"
    title="Financial aid"
    lede="Aid year 2026–27 covers students enrolled this year, including Fall Semester 2026 and Spring Semester 2027. This page is for that file."
    crumbs={[{ href: '/financial-aid/', label: 'Financial aid' }]}
  >
    <p class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn" href={u('/support/?category=financial-aid-hold#request')}>Submit an aid request</a>
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="prose wrap">
    <h2 id="overview">Aid year 2026–27</h2>
    <p>
      The University of Mars packages grants, work, and loans for undergraduates and graduate students who qualify. The
      aid year runs from summer 2026 through Spring Semester 2027. If you are enrolled now, this is your aid year.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your offer is posted in MyUM. Accept or decline each award before the term disburses. A grant left unaccepted does
      not pay, and it does not hold a place for later.
    </p>
    <h3>Cost of attendance, on-campus undergraduate</h3>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <caption class="sr-only">Estimated 2026–27 cost of attendance for an on-campus undergraduate</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Budget item</th>
            <th scope="col">In-state</th>
            <th scope="col">Nonresident</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Tuition and fees</th>
            <td>$13,940</td>
            <td>$44,210</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Housing and meals</th>
            <td>$16,480</td>
            <td>$16,480</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Books and supplies</th>
            <td>$1,120</td>
            <td>$1,120</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Personal and transportation</th>
            <td>$2,640</td>
            <td>$3,180</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>These figures are budgets, not a bill. Your housing contract and course fees can differ.</p>

    <h2 id="scholarships">Scholarships</h2>
    <p>
      Red Planet Scholars is the university’s principal need-based scholarship. It is offered with the grant package for
      aid year 2026–27. Departments name a smaller set of merit awards in March for the following year. Continuing
      students do not file a separate Red Planet Scholars application for 2026–27; the office uses the aid application
      already on file.
    </p>

    <h2 id="verification">How to complete verification</h2>
    <p>
      Each year the aid office selects a portion of files for verification. If you were selected for aid year 2026–27,
      MyUM shows a task, and a financial aid hold keeps aid from disbursing until the file is complete.
    </p>
    <p>
      Download and submit the <a href="#verification-worksheet">2026–27 Verification Worksheet</a>. Sign it, then send it
      with the tax documents listed below. Upload the packet through the Help Center under Financial aid hold, or bring
      it to the aid counter in Enrollment Services, 140 Olympus Way. The counter is open weekdays from 9 a.m. to 4 p.m.
    </p>
    <p id="verification-worksheet">
      Print the worksheet, sign it in ink, and include every page. Most complete packets are reviewed within ten
      business days. The office writes to your UM email when the hold is cleared or when a page is still missing.
    </p>

    <h2 id="documents">Required documents</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The signed worksheet</li>
      <li>A tax-return transcript, or a non-filing statement, for the student</li>
      <li>The same for each parent on a dependent file</li>
      <li>W-2 forms when the return reports wages</li>
      <li>A government ID only if a signature cannot be matched</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="holds">Holds explained</h2>
    <p>A hold can block registration, disbursement, or both. The comment on the hold names the office that placed it.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Financial aid hold.</strong> Usually a missing document, an unfinished verification file, or a
        satisfactory academic progress review. Aid for 2026–27 does not disburse while this hold is open.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Bursar hold.</strong> A past-due balance. See the billing article or call the cashier.</li>
      <li><strong>Registrar hold.</strong> A missing final transcript or an immunization record.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you dropped units after aid was paid, the award may be recalculated. Questions go through the
      <a href={u('/support/?category=financial-aid-hold#request')}>Help Center</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="dates">Key dates for 2026–27</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <caption class="sr-only">Key dates for aid year 2026–27</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Date</th>
            <th scope="col">What happens</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">February 15, 2026</th>
            <td>Priority filing date for aid year 2026–27. Late files are still reviewed.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">August 19, 2026</th>
            <td>Fall Semester disbursement for accepted awards.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Friday, November 20, 2026</th>
            <td>Last day to turn in a complete verification packet if you need spring payment on time.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Wednesday, January 6, 2027</th>
            <td>Spring Semester disbursement.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Friday, January 15, 2027</th>
            <td>Spring Semester 2027 add/drop deadline. Enrollment is locked for aid recalculation at the end of that day.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Monday, March 1, 2027</th>
            <td>Summer 2027 aid requests open for students already in a 2026–27 file.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <aside class="callout" id="next-year">
      <h2>Upcoming: aid year 2027–28</h2>
      <p>
        This block is only for next year’s applicants and for continuing students planning ahead. It does not change aid
        that is paying now for 2026–27.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The 2027–28 FAFSA and the state grant application opened October 1, 2026.</li>
        <li>University priority date for 2027–28: Monday, February 15, 2027.</li>
        <li>Offers for new Fall 2027 students begin going out in March 2027.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Students enrolled now should keep using the 2026–27 file.</p>
    </aside>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Student Financial Services<br />
      Enrollment Services, 140 Olympus Way<br />
      {site.locality}<br />
      <a href={site.aidHref}>{site.aidPhone}</a><br />
      <a href={`mailto:${site.aidEmail}`}>{site.aidEmail}</a><br />
      Weekdays, 9 a.m. to 4 p.m.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
